## Context

Ticket 0413 adopted the v2 reference and re-scored Experiments 1–3 (exp1_batch2
records + measurements rows, and the exp2_mart.jsonl / sota_cross_eval.csv arms).
It deliberately left the earlier **model-census** rows on v1-era scoring, with the
author's explicit agreement that full mart coherence is nice-to-have, not a
blocker for the v2 adoption PR.

While adopting v2, four pre-existing drifts surfaced (none v2-caused — all
predate 0413):

1. **Census rows not re-scored.** measurements.jsonl rows with
   `method ∈ {direct, rag, direct+multiturn}` (the pre-experiment census,
   "$5 burned on 26 models from memory") carry no `reference` field and still
   reflect v1-era scoring. Their raw replies live in
   `experiments/archive/outputs/{direct_extract,rag_extract,direct_multiturn,
   ablation,...}` — re-scoreable, but there is **no live DAG edge**: the
   `%.record.json: %.csv` pattern in score.mk resolves to `experiments/outputs/`,
   not `archive/`. An archive-sourced score path must be wired.
2. **Record/mart desync.** The committed `exp1_batch2/*.record.json` files and
   the committed measurements.jsonl disagreed on exp1 v1 scores (mart TP 2801 vs
   record TP 2894) before 0413. (0413's exp1 re-score incidentally fixed this for
   exp1; the broader desync class remains.)
3. **Stale census macros.** `tabulate_macros` regenerated from the current
   committed measurements yields `\NumModelsTested` 103 where committed
   macros.tex said 86 — the committed file was stale vs its own committed source.
4. **106 uncommitted-to-mart records.** `find … -name '*.record.json'` yields 668
   records on disk; the committed measurements.jsonl has 562 (frontier /
   direct_complete records present on disk, absent from the mart).

## Affected artifacts

- `macros_census.tex`, `macros_p1_base.tex`, `tab_census.tex` (`\input`'d by
  report.tex / slides — they currently render v1-era census numbers).
- Orphan figures `fig_scaling_curve.pdf`, `fig_regimes_scatter.pdf` (generated,
  not included in the manuscript) consume `result_summary.f1/tp` from census rows.
- The `prompt_version='census'` render path (`plot_method_convergence`,
  `tabulate_census_macros`) currently raises "No measurement records matched the
  active filter" against the committed measurements — broken at HEAD, not by 0413.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Wire an archive-sourced score path so census raw replies in
      `experiments/archive/outputs/` can be re-scored against v2 (no
      `rebuild-measurements`, which deletes records).
- [ ] Re-score census rows against v2; every re-scored measurements row carries
      `reference=vietnam_thermal_plants_v2_classified.csv`.
- [ ] Reconcile the committed mart with its committed sources (decide membership
      of the 106 extra records explicitly; row count documented, not accidental).
- [ ] Regenerate `macros_census` / `macros_p1_base` / `tab_census` / scaling /
      regimes from the v2-scored mart; centralize the `tabulate_macros`
      `ref_plants` constant via `evaluate.reference_plant_count()` (deferred from
      0413 to keep the census source+output revert mutually consistent).
- [ ] Manuscript reference-count propagation — GATED on two upstream settlements,
      do it once against the final state:
      (a) Exp3 (RAG) re-scored to v2 (this ticket) — unlocks the RAG recall
          *denominators* (`report.tex` §«Expérience 3 RAG» lines ~406/412/420/422/
          449/485). These stay LITERAL 163 until then because they are recall
          against still-v1 archived RAG data — `\NumRefPlants`=170 there would
          falsely claim 170/170 recall.
      (b) Plant count SETTLED by ticket 0445 (extension-as-unit vs standalone) —
          fixes the value `\NumRefPlants` resolves to (170 vs 174). Macroizing the
          reference-size mentions before 0445 risks doing it twice if the count
          moves.
      Then replace the literal `163` reference-size mentions with `\NumRefPlants`
      and update the recall numbers (`report.tex` §«Expérience direct complet»
      ~218, abstract ~49, conclusion ~669; `slides/manuscript/main.md` Exp1/Exp2
      captions if not already v2). 0413 already macro-ized the v2-coherent mentions
      (Exp2 provenance §269, reconciliation §396, slides §105) and applied the
      #547 de-inflation corrections to §396/§734.
- [ ] `make check` green.

